WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.001
-Yay!
-Hi.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.436
-Oh, it's so great to see you.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.705
Thank you so much for coming
back to our show.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.139
I appreciate this.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.608
-I'm so glad to be back,

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.377
and yeah, in this new format.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:15.081
-I heard that you're in
Australia, is that correct?

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:18.351
-I am in Sydney, yes,
ahead of shooting "Thor."

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.054
-How -- First of all,
how is Australia?

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.589
'Cause I've never been,
and I love it,

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.291
and everyone I know
who's Australian, I love.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.426
Everyone I've seen in movies --

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.095
I love "Muriel's Wedding."

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.997
I love everything about
Australia.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:34.400
But --
It's just gorgeous, right?

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.169
-It's a really amazing
country.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.205
I'm very -- I feel very,
very lucky to be here.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:42.141
The people are amazing,
and it's a beautiful --

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:43.977
And, yeah.
I don't know.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:45.845
You can you hear the birds,
like, singing right now?

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.414
-Yeah, that was almost on cue.
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:53.085
Whoever's helping you with
the sound effects, great job.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:55.288
Let me just explain to everyone
the time difference.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:58.090
Right now, it is Tuesday here
in America,

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.759
and it's Wednesday morning
where you are.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.794
So thank you for getting up
early to do this.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.830
-I'm in the future, yes.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.333
-Yeah, are we going to be
all right?

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.735
-It's all going to be okay,
Jimmy.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.970
-Thank you, thank you.
Thank you for saying that.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.772
How are you and the family?

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.674
How are you dealing
with quarantine

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.643
and all this stuff?

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.110
-We're good.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.147
You know, I think all of us
have had similar experiences

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.983
with kids at home during
quarantine.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.218
It's been --
-Yeah.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.854
-There are days when
things are great

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.756
and you're like,
I'm baking cupcakes

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.825
and we're doing crafts
and we're having a dance party.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.860
And then there are days that
you're like,

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.329
here's a screen and I'm going to
stare at the wall.

00:01:37.329 --> 00:01:39.498
And, you know, hope --

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.300
-Just go for it.
-Hope the day is over soon.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.702
-Yes. Download it.
Download it.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.404
I don't -- Yes.
Go for it. Go for it.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.671
-Yeah.
-I don't care, yeah.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.139
-I just kept looking at my
husband being like,

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:48.675
"Is it okay to have
a drink yet?"

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:50.477
Like, "What time is it?
Is it drink time?"

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.478
-"What time is it in America?"
-Yes.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.781
It's Tuesday night,
let's go for it.

00:01:55.781 --> 00:01:58.117
Can you talk about "Thor"?

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.619
I know we talked about it
a little bit

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.988
last time you were on,
and it's so secretive.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:06.359
-Um, yeah, I'm playing
the Mighty Thor,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:09.261
which is -- there were some
of the graphic novels

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:12.832
where Jane Foster becomes Thor.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.868
And it's going to be really,

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:18.838
like, silly and funny and great.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.706
We've got Taika Waititi
directing.

00:02:20.706 --> 00:02:22.841
-Taika Waititi is
brilliantly funny.

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:25.077
Oh, my gosh, is he talented.
-He's wonderful.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:28.080
So, I'm very excited to just
be working with --

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.515
-He has a good brain,
that guy.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.351
Are you actually filming
or are you still prepping?

00:02:32.351 --> 00:02:34.353
-Just prepping.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.389
-These movies, I don't
know if people understand

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.123
the training that goes into
these things.

00:02:38.123 --> 00:02:39.525
Did you have any idea?

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.727
I mean, are you doing these
crazy workouts and stuff?

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.463
Are you...

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.265
-I'm trying.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.733
-It's insane.
-I've also had like --

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.136
I've had, like, months of,
like, pandemic, you know,

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.239
eating baked goods
and, like, lying in bed

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.040
and feeling sorry for myself.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:59.678
-So it's -- I'm, like,
super tired after working out.

00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:00.780
-Yeah.
-And during.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.282
-Yeah.
-And dreading before.

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:05.017
-While you were in quarantine,
I also saw

00:03:05.017 --> 00:03:06.452
a couple things on Instagram.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.055
I follow you, you're a good
follow, by the way.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.456
There's many things you do.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.058
One that I'm obsessed with
is your cooking videos.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:14.527
I could watch you --

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.796
I could watch --
You should do a show.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.464
I would watch every single week.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.333
I would tune in.
I love it.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:25.071
It's like, it's so -- I just,
you got a knack for it.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.939
-Thank you.
That's so nice.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:30.443
I feel like I don't really
have a lot of skill.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:34.513
So I always feel like if I can
do it, anyone can do it.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:37.016
And feel like sharing those
things, 'cause I know

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:40.286
I've gotten so many great
recipes and stuff

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.289
from Instagram, from other
people that I follow.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.159
And it definitely
makes life easier

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.994
now that we're, like,
cooking every meal,

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.829
pretty much.
-Yeah, but no.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.731
It think I disagree.
I think you have skill.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.065
You know exactly --
-Thank you.

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.734
-I mean, everything is
chopped perfectly.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.270
I mean, it's just --
It's really, honestly,

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.273
I'm obsessed.
And it's also vegetarian,

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:03.542
or is it vegan, even?
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:06.813
I mean, I'm vegan,
and a lot of people think

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.815
we're, like, eating alfalfa,
you know, in the corner.

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:12.818
You know, so I like showing...
-No.

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:16.489
-...that there's really,
like, delicious, varied,

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:20.359
easy things that you can do
at home that your kids will eat

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.662
that are plant-based.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.830
And I've been lucky enough
to, like, learn a lot

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.466
from other people
I admire a lot.

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.768
-I love that part of,
you know,

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:31.904
I would say the silver lining
of all these things,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.906
but the quarantine, you know,
you go, "Oh, my gosh,

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:36.175
Natalie Portman, I love her,
she's my favorite actor."

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:39.212
And then you get to see more
of your personal side,

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.546
and you go, "Wait,
she's a great cook

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.047
and she's interested
in cooking."

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:45.218
You interview chefs, and like,
they're cooking with you.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.885
I was like --
I love that you did this.

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.954
Like, that's a gamble.
Like, you think your agent...

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.222
-Thank you.
-...would be like,

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:51.957
"Hey, just -- You're Thor.
We're good.

00:04:51.957 --> 00:04:54.160
We don't need to do this stuff.
Like, just --"

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.229
You know, and I love
that you did that.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.697
Not only that, I love
the book club, too.

00:04:58.697 --> 00:04:59.998
-Thanks.

00:04:59.998 --> 00:05:02.367
-How did that come about?

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.903
-Well, I love reading,

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:07.773
I love hearing from other people
what their recommendations are.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:11.110
So I started sharing what I was
reading and what I love.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.145
And it's great getting feedback
from people

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:15.080
and getting to read
alongside people

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.115
and hear what
their responses are.

00:05:17.115 --> 00:05:20.419
And it's been a really awesome
opportunity for me too

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:23.956
to get to meet some of the
writers that I really love

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.125
by getting to interview them
for the book club.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.428
It's kind of like an easy
pretext to talk to people

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.930
I really look up to.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.931
-Yeah, I want to talk to --

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:35.101
There's so many other things
I want to talk to you about.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.770
Over the summer, it was
announced that you

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.272
and some very other
accomplished women

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:41.641
are helping bring a brand new

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:45.477
women's professional soccer team
to L.A.

00:05:45.477 --> 00:05:48.180
That's massive.
-Thank you.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.816
-How do you get involved in
this, and how cool is that?

00:05:50.816 --> 00:05:53.352
You're like an owner
of a soccer team?

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:56.689
That's nuts.
-It's so exciting.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:06:01.560
A group of us became really
passionate about women's soccer

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.129
because we have the best players
in the world

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:05.464
in the United States,

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:07.667
in the most popular
sport in the world.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:13.639
And so we got together and we
are bringing Angel City FC,

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:19.478
the women's soccer team for
Los Angeles, to L.A. in 2022.

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:24.116
And we are super excited to
just kind of celebrate

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.918
these incredible athletes.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:30.856
And yeah, it's the first
female-led, female investors

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:33.926
of I think any
professional sport.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.928
-And I love the name, too.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.997
-Thanks.
-Yeah, I love it. I'm into it.

